'' A UDT both convertible by the target's CONSTRUCTOR and by its own 'operator cast': fbc runs
'' the constructor where the target is being constructed -- byval argument, initialiser,
'' return, new -- and the CAST everywhere else: byref argument, assignment, field and element
'' stores, an explicit cast( ). tiko ran the constructor for a byref argument and, for the
'' rest, copied A's own bytes into the B2 (overload re-pick refactor, Phase 3).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-conv-ctor-or-cast.bas -o tests/codegen/udtconvctororcast.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udtconvctororcast.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byval 300
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byref 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: init 300
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: assign 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: cast 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: return 300
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: field 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: elem 400
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: new 300
